0..76 Comment "// The simply typed lambda calculus as a theory whose terms are indexed by a"
77..150 Comment "// context and a type. Its syntax is a first-order model of the signature"
151..217 Comment "// (Kaposi and Xie, _Second-order generalised algebraic theories_,"
218..287 Comment "// doi:10.4230/LIPIcs.FSCD.2024.10). This source is the first rung of"
288..330 Comment "// normalisation by evaluation as a model."
331..333 Comment "//"
334..408 Comment "// The object types, the contexts, the variables and the terms are indexed"
409..484 Comment "// families. A renaming sends each variable of one context to a variable of"
485..560 Comment "// another. The semantic type of an arrow is the Kripke function space over"
561..620 Comment "// renamings. A recursion computes it from the object type."
621..623 Comment "//"
624..700 Comment "// The evaluator, reflection and reification stop at five refusals. The twin"
701..750 Comment "// in the pathological corpus names each of them."
751..753 Comment "//"
754..769 Comment "// - see: #5032"
